  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        518.4614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 28 December 1963 Randy Gardner, a 17-year-old science enthusiast at a San Diego high school, set out to forgo slumber for a regional science fair. Two companions diligently jolted him awake whenever his alertness waned and logged his mood. The project, a voluntary endeavour, went on to take first place."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        410.9614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.9614173228347
      ],
      "text": "William Dement, a sleep researcher at Stanford, read press coverage of the attempt and was intrigued. He drove to San Diego and assisted John J. Ross, a Navy researcher, in monitoring the sleepless boy closely. The two investigators attentively noted the fluctuations in his state as the deprivation progressively deepened."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        323.2614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        402.4614173228347
      ],
      "text": "The consequences soon mounted. Gardner grew moody, lost concentration, and found his short-term memory impaired. He became suspicious, at times paranoid, and began to hallucinate. On the fourth day he was gripped by the delusion that he was a professional American football player."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        215.7614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        314.7614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Gardner ended the wearying attempt on 8 January 1964, after 264.4 hours, about 11 days and 25 minutes. He then slept soundly for about 14 hours and woke apparently refreshed. Researchers probed the case in a 1965 scholarly paper, which helped highlight microsleeps, involuntary lapses into sleep lasting a few seconds. Gardner may have had such momentary bouts without noticing."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283468,
        461.8976377952756,
        207.2614173228347
      ],
      "text": "In 1997 Guinness World Records discontinued monitoring such attempts because of the health perils, and others have since alleged longer stints awake. In a 2017 interview Gardner said severe insomnia had tormented him for about a decade, and he himself pinned the blame on the experiment. The boy who had seemed to bounce back from exhaustion with one long rest would, decades later, barely doze off."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1963年12月28日，圣迭戈一名17岁的高中科学爱好者兰迪·加德纳，为了参加一场地区性的科学展，开始尝试放弃睡眠。两名同伴尽心尽力，每当他的警觉减弱，就让他猛然清醒过来，并记录了他的情绪。这个项目，一次自愿的尝试，继而夺得了第一名。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "威廉·德门特，斯坦福大学的睡眠研究者，读到了媒体对这次尝试的报道，并且非常感兴趣。他驾车前往圣迭戈，协助约翰·J·罗斯，一位海军研究员，去密切监视这个不眠的少年。两位研究人员专心地记下了他状态的种种波动，其间睡眠剥夺逐步加深。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        360.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "后果很快便开始不断加剧。加德纳变得喜怒无常，注意力难以集中，他的短时记忆也受损了。他变得多疑，有时甚至偏执/妄想性的，还开始出现幻觉。第四天，他被一种妄想/错觉攫住了，以为自己是一名美式橄榄球职业球员。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        252.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        352.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "加德纳于1964年1月8日结束了这场令人疲惫的尝试，共历时264.4小时，约合11天零25分钟。随后他酣畅地/深度地睡了约14小时，醒来时似乎神清气爽/恢复精神的。研究者们在1965年的一篇学术论文中探究了/深入研究这一案例，该论文有助于凸显微睡眠——指不由自主地陷入持续几秒钟短暂睡眠的状态。加德纳可能经历过这种短暂的发作而未曾察觉。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        163.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        243.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "1997年，吉尼斯世界纪录因健康风险停止了监测此类尝试；此后，其他人声称/宣称有过更长的清醒时段。在2017年的一次采访中，加德纳说严重的失眠折磨了他约十年，他本人把它归咎于这次实验。那个曾看似只要睡个长觉，就能从精疲力竭中迅速恢复的少年，几十年后，却几乎连打个盹都费劲。"
    }
  ],
